WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.383
(upbeat percussion music)

00:00:02.383 --> 00:00:05.908
- A bird in New York City
doesn't have it easy.

00:00:05.908 --> 00:00:09.177
Whether it's flying into a building,

00:00:09.177 --> 00:00:10.010
a car,

00:00:10.853 --> 00:00:12.155
a bicycle,

00:00:12.155 --> 00:00:14.264
dogs, pollution, lead poisoning.

00:00:14.264 --> 00:00:16.131
This is not nature's natural course.

00:00:16.131 --> 00:00:18.381
We have interfered with it.

00:00:22.672 --> 00:00:24.350
My name is Rita McMahon,

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:27.883
and I'm the co-founder and
director of the Wild Bird Fund.

00:00:27.883 --> 00:00:32.050
New York City's one and only
wildlife rehabilitation center.

00:00:35.437 --> 00:00:37.829
We take in birds that anyone has found,

00:00:37.829 --> 00:00:39.617
and we do our best to make it whole,

00:00:39.617 --> 00:00:42.534
so that it can go back to the wild.

00:00:44.127 --> 00:00:46.286
The atmosphere at the Wild
Bird Fund is something

00:00:46.286 --> 00:00:47.994
of a three-ring circus.

00:00:47.994 --> 00:00:50.556
There's the iso room, the waterfowl room,

00:00:50.556 --> 00:00:55.102
reception area, and downstairs
is a whole 'nother thing.

00:00:55.102 --> 00:00:58.514
There are couple of
hundred birds down there.

00:00:58.514 --> 00:01:00.097
They may be flying around in the air

00:01:00.097 --> 00:01:02.091
as people are scurrying around.

00:01:02.091 --> 00:01:05.721
Cleaning the cages, giving
them meds, and feeding them.

00:01:05.721 --> 00:01:09.212
We deal with 135 different species,

00:01:09.212 --> 00:01:13.926
this past week we had a
Canada goose, seven kestrels,

00:01:13.926 --> 00:01:17.499
a rowdy bunch of juvenile herring gulls.

00:01:17.499 --> 00:01:21.666
This year, 2016, we will
treat well over 4,000 birds.

00:01:25.514 --> 00:01:28.602
By being in New York City
where the animal is found,

00:01:28.602 --> 00:01:31.938
we are able to save many more animals.

00:01:31.938 --> 00:01:34.987
They would die before they
could get help in another state

00:01:34.987 --> 00:01:36.731
or another county.

00:01:36.731 --> 00:01:40.232
People can come to you via subway or bus

00:01:40.232 --> 00:01:42.548
and they can get the animal to you faster.

00:01:42.548 --> 00:01:45.105
It's exciting, you never
really know who's gonna walk

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:49.258
through that door, or what
they're holding in that box.

00:01:49.258 --> 00:01:52.317
- I was at my store and I saw the pigeon.

00:01:52.317 --> 00:01:54.911
I saw that he was like bleeding
on the floor like pretty bad.

00:01:54.911 --> 00:01:57.460
I didn't even know that
they took in pigeons.

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:00.113
- [Rita] It's okay, it's okay.

00:02:00.113 --> 00:02:03.196
(gentle piano music)

00:02:04.367 --> 00:02:08.534
Any animal that is picked
up is in really bad shape.

00:02:10.823 --> 00:02:14.481
50% will die or are euthanized.

00:02:14.481 --> 00:02:19.356
If we can reduce the suffering,
that's a good thing too.

00:02:19.356 --> 00:02:21.106
But 50% go free.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:23.957
When the bird's better,

00:02:25.005 --> 00:02:28.822
you try to return it to where it came.

00:02:28.822 --> 00:02:31.543
If it's an adult bird, it
might have family, friends,

00:02:31.543 --> 00:02:34.022
it knows where to live.

00:02:34.022 --> 00:02:36.632
The migratory birds, they're
just passing through,

00:02:36.632 --> 00:02:37.790
you're really just trying to put them

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:38.954
in a safe place so that they can

00:02:38.954 --> 00:02:40.871
continue their journey.

